Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:07:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): count effective lane admissions and expire stale
 skips [daveey]

Review 5990728120 found two PR behavior defects at e5b7280382.
Why the cap failed open: enforcement mapped unknown tenants to the default lane,
but admission accounting compared their raw event lane. Map current and legacy
admission receipts with the same policy and preserve distinct-card accounting,
re-lane exclusion and local midnight. Thread explicit report/enforcement policies.
Why running cards showed quota: historical dispatch skips outlived claims and
launches and were evaluated before running state. End skip observations at
claim/launch/completion/reopen boundaries; inspect only the latest skip and
prefer running over dispatch-wait evidence.

Proof: 10 new persisted regression failures on reviewed head; 14 now green,
including operator's exact reproductions, alias/legacy/midnight and current-skip
controls. Nine consumer files: 189 passed, 0 failed. Eight mutants killed with
14-test unmutated baseline; full scripts/check: 21 checks ok. Read-only replay
of hub boards and sync-shadow daily admission rows found zero changed raw-lane
mappings (default shadow 400 rows, hub default 252). No production caps enabled.
